  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=a|\\sin x|+b e^{|x|}+c|x|^3$, where $a, b, c \\in R$, is differentiable at $x=0$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KVoq3",
      "text": "\n$a=0, b$ and $c$ are any real numbers\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hcv8v",
      "text": "\n$c=0, a=0, b$ is any real number\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2VhjG",
      "text": "\n$b=0, c=0, a$ is any real number\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "39TmG",
      "text": "\n$a=0, b=0, c$ is any real number",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$|\\sin x|$ and $e^{|x|}$ are not differentiable at $x=0$ and $|x|^3$ is differentiable at $x=0$. $\\therefore$ for $f(x)$ to be differentiable at $x=0$, we must have $a=0, b=0$ and $c$ is any real number.",
    "image": null
  },
